440 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 119 0 R
/T (In this plot the 3 K-Means clusters sit next to each other and touch at the borders, they are not separate islands. Cluster 0 \(red\) is the big group at the lower left, cluster 2 \(green\) is in the middle going to the right, and cluster 1 \(blue\) is the sparse group in the upper part. This matches the silhouette score of 0.308, which means the clusters are there but they overlap. Also, PC1 and PC2 only explain about 45% of the variance, so some of the overlap may just be because of the 2D view.)
/E (In this plot the 3 K-Means clusters sit next to each other and touch at the borders, they are not separate islands. Cluster 0 \(red\) is the big group at the lower left, cluster 2 \(green\) is in the middle going to the right, and cluster 1 \(blue\) is the sparse group in the upper part. This matches the silhouette score of 0.308, which means the clusters are there but they overlap. Also, PC1 and PC2 only explain about 45% of the variance, so some of the overlap may just be because of the 2D view.)
/Pg 21 0 R
