1204 0 obj
<<
/Title (The data has 3999 customers and 12 columns \(shape printed in Task 1 of the notebook\), taken from the East-West Airlines workbook. The Description sheet of that workbook says that the key issues are the customers' flying patterns, how they earn and use frequent flyer rewards, and their use of the airline credit card, and that the task is to identify customer segments via clustering. The three algorithms I used are K-Means, Hierarchical clustering and DBSCAN.)
