<<
/Title (complete, average and single give very high silhouette scores \(0.5 to 0.68\), which looks great at first, but look at the cluster sizes: the biggest cluster has 3700+ customers out of 3815 and the smallest ones have only 1 to 8 customers. So these methods just pick a few extreme customers and put them in their own tiny clusters, and everyone else is in one giant cluster. The high silhouette is misleading here, and this is not a useful segmentation.)
